    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "description": "Distribution opsdir-adapter-jira-sm (import opsdir_adapter_jira_sm), registered via entry point opsdir.adapters:jira-sm; depends on opsdir.",
        "external_dependencies": "[\"Jira REST API (GET /rest/api/3|2/issue/{key}, /rest/api/3|2/field, read-only)\", \"Jira Service Management REST API (GET /rest/servicedeskapi/request/{key}/approval, read-only)\", \"Jira REST API create issue body (POST /rest/api/3|2/issue: drafted as files a person posts, never called)\"]",
        "path": "packages/opsdir-adapter-jira-sm/",
        "purpose": "Jira Service Management as an ITSM add-on (kind itsm): reads the change tickets the record's change records link (jira-sm:<KEY>) as evidence, and drafts the work tickets handing a team its findings. Importer jira-sm/change-requests reads REST answers (issues, approvals, field list) through the operator's mapping settings jira-sm-status-states and jira-sm-change-fields; an issue of jira-sm-ticket-issue-type is read back as a work ticket (kind work, due day, no approval). A read-only collector makes one GET per linked issue plus its approval pages (Cloud v3 or Data Center v2; none for work tickets). Adapter.ticket_draft (drafts.py) writes a Task issue create body (Cloud v3 ADF / Data Center v2 wiki) per team from jira-sm-ticket-site, -projects, -team-field, -issue-type, -fields; opsdir posts nothing."
      },
      "kind": "modules",
      "op": "modify",
      "semantic_key": {
        "name": "adapter-jira-sm"
      }
    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "file": "packages/opsdir-adapter-jira-sm/src/opsdir_adapter_jira_sm/changes.py",
        "id_in_name": 1,
        "name": "ticket_facts",
        "parameters": "[{\"name\": \"issue\", \"type\": \"dict\", \"required\": true}, {\"name\": \"steps\", \"type\": \"tuple[dict] | None\", \"required\": true, \"description\": \"its approval steps; None when the export holds none or stops before the last page\"}, {\"name\": \"states\", \"type\": \"dict[str, str]\", \"required\": true}, {\"name\": \"fields\", \"type\": \"dict[str, str]\", \"required\": true, \"description\": \"{role: field id}\"}, {\"name\": \"work\", \"type\": \"bool\", \"required\": false, \"description\": \"a work ticket (an issue of jira-sm-ticket-issue-type); default False\"}]",
        "purpose": "The ticket attributes (governance TICKET_ATTRS) of one Jira issue and its approval steps through the operator's mapping: summary, issue id as ciamProviderRef, its self URL, neutral state, overall approval, native status, neutral change type, windows from the mapped fields, step rows, approver rows, facts (issuetype, status category, resolution, created, updated, other mapped fields); for a work ticket (work=True) ciamTicketKind work and ciamTicketDue from duedate, and no approval, steps, approvers or change type; with the problems of window values that aren't date-times, a duedate that isn't a day and change types that aren't neutral.",
        "returns": "{\"type\": \"tuple\", \"description\": \"({attribute: value or tuple or None}, (problem, ...))\"}",
        "source_hash": "743f8d1656775163"
      },
      "kind": "functions",
      "op": "modify",
      "semantic_key": {
        "entity_key": "fn-ticket-facts-d5062e41"
      }
    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "file": "packages/opsdir-adapter-jira-sm/src/opsdir_adapter_jira_sm/changes.py",
        "id_in_name": 1,
        "name": "read_changes",
        "parameters": "[{\"name\": \"files\", \"type\": \"dict[str, str]\", \"required\": true}, {\"name\": \"d\", \"type\": \"Directory\", \"required\": true}, {\"name\": \"patterns\", \"type\": \"tuple\", \"required\": true}, {\"name\": \"at\", \"type\": \"datetime | None\", \"required\": false, \"description\": \"when the export was taken (required)\"}]",
        "purpose": "Importer jira-sm/change-requests: each linked issue the export holds (REST answers: issues, search answers, approval pages, the field list), its own import group under ou=jira-sm,ou=tickets, through the operator's mapping settings; an issue of the work issue type (jira-sm-ticket-issue-type) is read as a work ticket (kind work, due day, no approval); notices for mapping problems, unmapped statuses and window fields (with the site's candidates, change tickets only), fields never carried, unlinked issues, linked ones missing (never removed), approvals missing or short of their last page (change tickets only), values that aren't times, error answers, files that aren't answers, several sites (refused), and the count read (with work tickets).",
        "returns": "{\"type\": \"Imported\"}",
        "source_hash": "8bccebdf0d875b50"
      },
      "kind": "functions",
      "op": "modify",
      "semantic_key": {
        "entity_key": "fn-read-changes-4b1885a2"
      }
    },
